{
  "_readme": {
    "workflow": "Set a biome's \"multiplier\" (or \"replace_with\"), then /reload or rejoin to see the solve (result_pct / note below update), and create a NEW world to use it. kubejs/server_scripts/worldgen/biome_overrides.js solves the layout at every world load. Multipliers other than 0/1 need a climate sample from /dumpclimate first (see README.md).",
    "multiplier": "1.0 = untouched. 0 = removed (its climate space goes to whichever biomes border it). 0.5 = half as common, 2.0 = twice as common, measured against share_pct. The solver hits these by raising/lowering one offset penalty per biome, so a boosted biome grows outward from its existing patches into its climate neighbours, never appears somewhere climatically unrelated.",
    "replace_with": "A biome id, or null. Relabels every entry of this biome to that one -- an exact swap of the same climate space. Overrides multiplier.",
    "read_only": "\"entries\" (how many climate boxes the biome owns), \"layer\" (surface or underground -- which sample layer its share is measured on), \"share_pct\" (original % of that layer), \"result_pct\" (% after the last solve), \"note\" (solver warnings, e.g. target clamped).",
    "caveat": "Every world stores its biome layout in level.dat at creation time. Changes only affect worlds created AFTER the override exists; existing saves keep the layout they were made with."
  },
